<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:28:14Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump envoys, European officials to discuss ‘new ideas’ for Ukraine peace in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ce901149dab2a12e19acf17e0ba1983be0bd888e5ae418645b9d064a8f73499</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T21:19:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-trump-envoys-ukraine-peace-talks-miami--619d0e85a342.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-trump-envoys-ukraine-peace-talks-miami" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump’s envoys will meet Ukrainian negotiators and European officials in Miami on Friday to discuss new proposals to end Russia’s war in Ukraine, two US sources told AFP. Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner will present ideas developed during recent talks with both sides, one source said Thursday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Black sea and black ops: How exposed is Europe to Ukraine war spillover?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60c51bcc3ba01dd796fb56d997c6030f0051c012b3e25254c58b63d42375aeeb</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T20:42:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261008-black-sea-and-black-ops-how-exposed-is-europe-to-ukraine-war-spillover--b0bb3b79e51f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261008-black-sea-and-black-ops-how-exposed-is-europe-to-ukraine-war-spillover" /><summary type="html">The story’s as underreported as it is consequential for the entire planet: Three Turkish-owned cargo ships out of Ukraine hit in EU waters by suspected Russian drones. One, the Togo-flagged Alfa Watan sinking Tuesday off Bulgaria. Ten Egyptian and Syrian crew missing. For its part, Ukraine’s been hitting Russian tankers in the Black Sea... this with no sign of a return to a UN-brokered deal to allow oil, grain and fertilizer ships to pass.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Spain mourns Maricarmen Abascal, whose eviction sparked housing protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df77f190fd2b8bd4983f5b4d91a1821f2e57b0bb17b2397898bc5543af37ceb3</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T20:35:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-mourns-maricarmen-abascal-whose-eviction-sparked-housing-protests--91508a8d7343.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-mourns-maricarmen-abascal-whose-eviction-sparked-housing-protests" /><summary type="html">Protests and anger have grown across Spain after the death of an 87-year-old woman in the wake of her eviction from her home. Maricarmen Abascal was thrown out of her home of seven decades in what became the "cause celebre" of Spain's housing crisis. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Two Latvian men arrested at UK base housing US and NATO intelligence hubs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0dd765b0989005406894e183c9514490636b417e380f9c47a99281a4b14dd7f</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:57:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-two-latvian-men-arrested-at-uk-base-housing-us-and-nato-intelligence-hubs--393dadf82f17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-two-latvian-men-arrested-at-uk-base-housing-us-and-nato-intelligence-hubs" /><summary type="html">British ​counter-terrorism police are investigating after two Latvian men were arrested Thursday near a Royal Air Force ​base in southeast England housing US and NATO intelligence operations, police said in a statement. The arrests come days after a major incident at another UK base led the US military to withdraw B-1 bombers stationed there.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French, US and Russian astronauts return to Earth after eight months in space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b81be6e977f6696b16bee2e1e479babb9be4c4a193e4a87dffd695215ce8416</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:02:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-french-us-and-russian-astronauts-return-to-earth-after-eight-months-in-space--ded2d2b5229c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-french-us-and-russian-astronauts-return-to-earth-after-eight-months-in-space" /><summary type="html">SpaceX brought France's Sophie Adenot and fellow astronauts Jessica Meir, Jack Hathaway and Andrey Fedyaev back to Earth on Thursday after an eight-month mission on board the International Space Station that saw Adenot become the first French woman to walk in space.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Search warrants for former prince Andrew's homes were unlawful, UK court rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e04a7c6781fe725cc83a7a48f7165da351b2136948064572a401b8efee6a5f3</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:09:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-search-warrants-for-former-prince-andrew-homes-were-unlawful-uk-court-rules--df9bf5d6c48d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-search-warrants-for-former-prince-andrew-homes-were-unlawful-uk-court-rules" /><summary type="html">Police who searched the properties of Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor as part of investigations into his links to the late sex offender Jeffrey Epstein have agreed the search warrants were unlawful, a London judge said Thursday. The 66-year-old younger brother of King Charles II was arrested on February 19 on suspicion of misconduct in public office.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>New Paris exhibition explores Ireland's housing crisis through contemporary art</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b95aec670711f2eeeac799836416f20f3f7d90eb4bd75a645ddd5e3d58435e36</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:26:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:29:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261008-new-paris-exhibition-explores-ireland-s-housing-crisis-through-contemporary-art--34e2c2f9b707.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261008-new-paris-exhibition-explores-ireland-s-housing-crisis-through-contemporary-art" /><summary type="html">Huge demonstrations have been held over the last few weeks in Spain over its housing crisis, but the issue is not restricted to Spain. Many other countries also have a huge problem with housing, including Ireland, with experts saying that for every street of 10 houses, the country actually needs 12. Now a new exhibition in Paris at the Irish Cultural Centre is trying to reflect the issue. In Perspective, we spoke to the museum's director and one of the artists taking part.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Maricarmen, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction shook Spain, dies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b9813f433f3210d09d9372e8c9068b9ec2ca5ee9ac60a45d359bcf4cff3b305</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:27:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:54:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-maricarmen-the-87-year-old-woman-whose-eviction-shook-spain-dies--c9a94189bc69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-maricarmen-the-87-year-old-woman-whose-eviction-shook-spain-dies" /><summary type="html">María del Carmen Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction from her longtime Madrid home sparked nationwide protests across Spain and unleashed a political crisis, died on Wednesday while hospitalised.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in Literature awarded to Canada’s Anne Carson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92ca21bad1ad46cd0589c0f1f4065ff06482663ef28ac34d6b99708d87aee506</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:27:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:04:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-nobel-prize-in-literature-awarded-to-canada-anne-carson--e2bf3cfdb309.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-nobel-prize-in-literature-awarded-to-canada-anne-carson" /><summary type="html">The Nobel Prize in Literature was awarded to Canadian poet and essayist Anne Carson on Thursday by the Swedish Academy in Stockholm. Toronto-born Carson, 76, draws from ancient Greek and Roman literature for her works blending elements of poetry, essay and fiction. She will receive 12 million Swedish kronor (about $1.2 million) alongside the prestigious award.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Evicted pensioner Maricarmen, symbol of Spain's housing crisis, dies at 87</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdf87031bc6678da20fae7c92be99f651c0073b96071138aebd5a04f1e8d7470</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:27:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:35:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261008-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-symbol-of-spain-s-housing-crisis-dies-at-87--2674a49e3c93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261008-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-symbol-of-spain-s-housing-crisis-dies-at-87" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 8: Maricarmen, the evicted Spanish pensioner who became the face of Spain's housing crisis, dies in hospital. Also, France braces for "Act Four" of high school student protests against dilapidated schools and poor staff presence. Finally, actress Zendaya sparks a row over etiquette at Paris Fashion Week.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>More than 30 killed in Russian strike on buses in Ukraine's Kramatorsk as Kyiv targets data centre</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f76bdd266e60f4ed8ca383767f38cc5faaf44a5bc8fb2faad7dbdc2f3999e9dd</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:27:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:08:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-russian-strike-buses-kills-at-least-12-ukraine-kramatorsk-kyiv-targets-data-centre--51d9e9f09beb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-russian-strike-buses-kills-at-least-12-ukraine-kramatorsk-kyiv-targets-data-centre" /><summary type="html">At least 30 people were killed in a Russian strike on two buses in the Ukrainian city of Kramatorsk in the eastern Donetsk region on Thursday. Earlier, a drone hit a data centre belonging to Russian technology company Yandex, causing a fire.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Evicted pensioner who sparked Spain housing protests dies: tenant union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7df6f0fde219afa2cd8101c349f01155aa926ad74df12ed7b8802c1225443372</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:27:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T20:14:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/evicted-pensioner-who-sparked-spain-housing-protests-dies-tenant-union--1e82e99df62b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/evicted-pensioner-who-sparked-spain-housing-protests-dies-tenant-union" /><summary type="html">Maricarmen ​Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction sparked housing ​protests in Spain, has died, Madrid's tenants' union said on Wednesday. Abascal's eviction sparked a series of ​protests ‌across Spain in the past couple ⁠of weeks, including activists camping on one of Madrid's main ‌squares, and calls for tackling a ⁠mounting housing crisis. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Evicted pensioner Maricarmen Abascal, heart of Spain's housing protests, dies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a4a204fc8105754fe7c4d4161a0c79be5d49932614c2fbd4f4c472a616b219e</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:27:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T19:19:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-abascal-heart-of-spain-housing-protests-has-died--aad131e25ae3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-abascal-heart-of-spain-housing-protests-has-died" /><summary type="html">Maricarmen ​Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction sparked housing ​protests in Spain, has died, Madrid's tenants' union said on Wednesday. Massive protests following Abascal's eviction spiralled into a political crisis, eventually leading Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez to call a snap election.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What we know about espionage, treason allegations against Germany's ex-spy chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ee42bfea320a34750f34e48c29b5a18d4e019ae52402714d7f2f71ba0969755</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:27:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T14:06:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-what-we-know-about-espionage-treason-allegations-against-germany-s-ex-spy-chief--62458e57ed6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-what-we-know-about-espionage-treason-allegations-against-germany-s-ex-spy-chief" /><summary type="html">A court on Wednesday ordered the former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service August Hanning to remain in pretrial detention after his arrest on suspicion of espionage and treason, along with a former deputy who allegedly supplied him with secret files. Here's what we know about one of the biggest security breaches in German history.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia warns against spreading 'false information' as reports emerge of second plague case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8311cf194c16486a14f74a053e5e9c5a98e97a6cf03cf436fc5aefa36ec91577</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:27:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:43:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-russia-warns-against-spreading-false-information-reports-emerge-second-plague-case--88e142bb04b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-russia-warns-against-spreading-false-information-reports-emerge-second-plague-case" /><summary type="html">The World Health Organization joined Western leaders on Wednesday in urging Russia to share more information about what killed a plague institute worker in Siberia as reports emerged of a second suspected case. The Kremlin said Moscow had shared what it knew and accused the media ​of spreading "false information".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in Chemistry awarded to France's Henri Kagan, Japan's Kenso Soai</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e1441d353a9d7135d4425cdd160456b0b00c751104b12badf8152f439691383</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:27:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:52:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-nobel-prize-in-chemistry-jointly-awarded-to-france-s-henri-kagan-japan-s-kenso-soai--fa8fe9233912.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-nobel-prize-in-chemistry-jointly-awarded-to-france-s-henri-kagan-japan-s-kenso-soai" /><summary type="html">Henri Kagan and Kenso Soai were jointly awarded the Nobel Prize in Chemistry for solving a 100-year-old chemical mystery, the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences said on Wednesday. Nobel Prize recipients receive a prize of 12 million Swedish kronor (about $1.2 million).</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Politkovskaya 'predicted' Russia's turn under Putin, editor says on 20th anniversary of her death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e2dc5d598d885f6b44129ae67cf1baa5767a499c56e06d4bd51b673cbcd5f96</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:28:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T08:32:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-anna-politkovskaya-the-slain-reporter-who-predicted-russia-future--bc157562a726.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-anna-politkovskaya-the-slain-reporter-who-predicted-russia-future" /><summary type="html">Assassinated Russian journalist Anna Politkovskaya "predicted" Moscow's trajectory under President Vladimir Putin 20 years ago,  her former editor said ahead of the anniversary of her death on Wednesday. Politkovskaya had reported on the war in Chechnya and Putin's rise before she was gunned down in her Moscow apartment block on October 7, 2006.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia launches one of its biggest strikes on Ukraine, killing at least 21 civilians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:978eb8187b7c1d1e2d8f022e30e5d007fc00827dae74c42e59651656758b1fb1</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:28:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T05:56:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-at-least-two-killed-in-fire-caused-by-massive-strikes-on-kyiv--e5db15870a76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-at-least-two-killed-in-fire-caused-by-massive-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Russian missiles and drones killed at least 21 people in Ukraine, including four children, in what President Volodymyr Zelensky ‌called a “massive” strike on Wednesday. Ukraine has come under increased attack in recent weeks as Russian attacks have targeted energy infrastructure and rail and road transport.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says will speak with Putin over Russia's reported plague death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47d09a84c16d8d0510f460874dae95b79b08d076dfccfa1a4ea826f94fdd4c18</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:28:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T22:51:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-trump-says-he-will-speak-to-putin-over-reported-plague-death-in-russia--66e579341611.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-trump-says-he-will-speak-to-putin-over-reported-plague-death-in-russia" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Tuesday he would speak “very soon” with Russian President Vladimir Putin over the reported death from plague of a laboratory technician, as Washington and the World Health Organization pressed Moscow for greater transparency and clarity over conflicting accounts of the incident in Siberia.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's former spy chief detained on suspicion of trading state secrets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b86ce5d5f1f658a6f5c1eac44e9351e509f76cbe131f4945cd2617ef204d1e7c</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:28:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T21:34:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-former-german-spy-chief-detained-over-suspected-treasonous-espionage--2b6da42acbed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-former-german-spy-chief-detained-over-suspected-treasonous-espionage" /><summary type="html">Former German spy chief August Hanning was detained Tuesday on suspicion of treason and espionage after prosecutors accused him of paying for secret intelligence documents and using them to prepare an analysis for a foreign intelligence service, in a case that could strain Berlin’s ties with allied spy agencies.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian lab worker's death sparks plague fears as unverified claims spread online</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9851cc4612a85c3d08f501ecda5714863fa2bd5222df48f1056702d48819326</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:28:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T20:58:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261006-russian-lab-worker-s-death-sparks-plague-fears-as-unverified-claims-spread-online-1--fec785980ee7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261006-russian-lab-worker-s-death-sparks-plague-fears-as-unverified-claims-spread-online-1" /><summary type="html">The death of a 28-year-old Russian lab worker at Siberia's Irkutsk Anti-Plague Research Institute has sparked online panic about a "plague, despite the WHO assessing the public health risk in Russia as low. Unverified claims about how the worker became ill, including a laboratory accident involving a test tube, are circulating online. Misleading posts and out-of-context videos have also fuelled speculation and fear. Vedika Bahl goes through them, and what we know, in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Police make seventh arrest over UK airbase incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fe897b333372b65f7faac137b1b9b49d2891d6e305d624d9adc9221ac51f893</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:24:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:51:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident--a2cfc3b816d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident" /><summary type="html">A seventh man was arrested Tuesday over a major incident last month at a British military airbase used by the United States to launch strikes on Iran, police said. The arrest came a day after President Donald Trump said the United States had withdrawn all B-1 bombers from RAF Fairford because of "threats" he believed were linked to Tehran. A 22-year-old British male was arrested in London "on suspicion of preparation of terrorist acts", Britain's Counter-Terrorism Policing network said in a statement. Six men in their 20s have already been arrested and released on bail after three suspicious vans were stopped near the base in southwest England on September 27. FRANCE 24's Bénédicte Paviot reports from London.</summary></entry><entry><title>German ex-spy chief arrested for suspected espionage, treason</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51cd46b7f870efa0e033ac4ee6573d7d6dec240023020877c4605fbd51a0abfe</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:24:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:42:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason--cbca89fe2a12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason" /><summary type="html">A former German spy chief was arrested Tuesday on suspicion of espionage and treason, an embarrassing case at a time when the country is seeking to broaden the powers of its intelligence agencies. August Hanning, who ran Germany's BND foreign intelligence agency from 1998 to 2005, is accused of espionage, treason and working for foreign intelligence services, federal prosecutors said. FRANCE 24's Nick Holdsworth reports from Berlin.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Busification': Inside Ukraine’s controversial recruitment practices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e4fdd6f71dd86c5c30893f6da40f29ae8a30e41028bf161060453b6ae7bee75</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:24:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:19:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-busification-inside-ukraine-s-controversial-recruitment-practices--28bf4e6cdcb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-busification-inside-ukraine-s-controversial-recruitment-practices" /><summary type="html">Recent reports and videos of alleged recruitment irregularities are fuelling tensions between mobilisation authorities and Ukrainian society, while raising questions about the oversight and implementation of military recruitment.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK police arrest 22-year-old British man in suspected Fairford base plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db165f480915dfdf7b424289e60659463bfb02bddd0e4497b9631916d46ef09f</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:24:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:26:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-uk-police-make-new-arrest-in-suspected-air-base-plot--cc7e5c5471a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-uk-police-make-new-arrest-in-suspected-air-base-plot" /><summary type="html">UK ​police on Tuesday said they had ​arrested ‌a ⁠22-year ‌old British man ⁠in London on suspicion ​of preparing terrorist acts ‌in relation ​to the suspected plot at the ​RAF ​Fairford ​airbase used ​by the US to strike Iran.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Catalan separatist Puigdemont cleared to return to Spain after court lifts arrest warrant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1655198dcba6b2b021be973a6ad8431bb3558d99d9d218822b99eea15d42fafd</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:24:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:10:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-exiled-catalan-separatist-leader-puigdemont-cleared-to-return-to-spain--8ba16e2f1ed9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-exiled-catalan-separatist-leader-puigdemont-cleared-to-return-to-spain" /><summary type="html">A Spanish Supreme Court judge on Tuesday lifted the arrest warrant for Catalan separatist leader Carles Puigdemont, clearing the way for him to return home without fear of detention ahead of a general election in November.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Philip Ingram sees Russia, China and Iran stepping up 'grey zone' activities across UK and Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2d416f34f694044e94c9f8c4cdc680e6bd32f224ae97f79002332fc053c0ffc</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:28:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:13:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261006-philip-ingram-sees-russia-china-and-iran-stepping-up-gray-zone-activities-across-uk-and-eur--f068b3b762fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261006-philip-ingram-sees-russia-china-and-iran-stepping-up-gray-zone-activities-across-uk-and-europe" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Philip Ingram, journalist and former British military intelligence officer. The events surrounding RAF Fairford are not an isolated incident, Ingram explains. They are part of a much wider security issue in which conventional military operations, intelligence activity and "grey zone" tactics increasingly overlap.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Should we be worried about a plague outbreak in Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3db76db2abc123b334286f3088ab3697288e57a4351fdcc38dece50ba24caad7</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:24:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:30:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261006-should-we-be-worried-about-a-plague-outbreak-in-russia--38fad56138a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261006-should-we-be-worried-about-a-plague-outbreak-in-russia" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, October 6: The death of a researcher in Siberia, reportedly from the plague, sparks concern despite Russian authorities' denial. But first: French high school protesters are promising "Act 3" of their protest movement against learning conditions. Also, Le Monde speaks to the editor of Russian independent outlet Novaya Gazeta ahead of the 20th anniversary of the murder of investigative journalist Anna Politkovskaya. Finally, it appears that butter is back in fashion.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria searches for missing crew as drones hit two Black Sea ships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2d60ec95dbe6fe4a6fc435febb3fc49b98bf0853b291e95a3299574c5187fbb</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:24:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:24:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-bulgaria-searches-for-missing-crew-as-drones-hit-two-more-black-sea-ships--a9c664076180.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-bulgaria-searches-for-missing-crew-as-drones-hit-two-more-black-sea-ships" /><summary type="html">Bulgarian authorities on Tuesday launched a search for missing crew members of a boat that sank in its economic zone in the Black Sea after drones hit two merchant vessels. Black Sea shipping has been hit by growing fallout from the war in Ukraine in recent months.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine hits Moscow with one of its largest drone attacks in two years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:644defbddc21bd67af4bb300d04c31e29def769736dffaf35b7cc88ab8d5c982</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:24:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T06:11:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-massive-ukrainian-drone-attack-targets-moscow-russian-officials-say--d7ae0a7240b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-massive-ukrainian-drone-attack-targets-moscow-russian-officials-say" /><summary type="html">Ukraine launched overnight one of its largest drone attacks on Moscow in the past two years, killing two men and injuring several people in the Russian capital, local officials said on Tuesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
